<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shanghai Municipal Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1854">1854</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> Municipal Council was the governing body of the Shanghai International Settlement from 1854 to 1943. Elected by foreign ratepayers and dominated by British businessmen, it ran the settlement's police, public works, health services and volunteer corps with little Chinese representation. It was dissolved when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> gave up their extraterritorial rights in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 1943.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shanghai-municipal-council.jpg" alt="Shanghai Municipal Council" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ericmetro and others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Shanghai_International_Settlement_pre-WWI.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
